\group groups instruments on the score, connecting their
staves with bar lines at the end of every bar.
Its syntax is the following:

\group \inst1 \inst2 \inst3

The instruments must be adjacent, and given in the order
they appear on the score, otherwise it throws an error.

An optional name can be given as the last argument, without
the backslash. This creates a command for the group, which
passes whatever follows it to every instrument of the group:

\group \hat \snare \kick drums

\drums rhythm

The line above turns all three instruments to rhythmic ones.
Methods are passed to the instruments too:

\drums.transpose 2

\group takes at least two instruments, and when only two
arguments are given, both must be instruments. A group name
can't be the name of a LiveLily command.
